.TH CPM_DISK 1 "2026-11-24" "cpmemu" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cpm_disk \- make, read and change CP/M disk images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cpm_disk
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.I disk
.RI [ files ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cpm_disk
makes CP/M disk images, and copies files into them and out of them.
It reads and writes three formats:
.TP
.B hd1k
The RomWBW hd1k format: one 8MB slice.
This is the default.
.TP
.B sssd
An 8\-inch single\-sided single\-density floppy (ibm\-3740), 250KB.
.TP
.B combo
A RomWBW combo disk: a 1MB prefix with an MBR, then six 8MB hd1k slices
(51MB).
.B \-\-slice
selects a slice, and a slice works as a plain hd1k image.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "create " disk
Make an empty disk image.
.TP
.BI "add " "disk files" ...
Copy host files into the image.
.TP
.BI "list " disk
List the files in the image, with the F1 to F8, R/O, SYS and ARC attributes
that are set.
.TP
.BI "delete " "disk files" ...
Delete files from the image.
.TP
.BI "extract " "disk files" ...
Copy files from the image to the host.
.TP
.BI "read\-boot " "disk output"
Copy the boot area of the image to the host file
.IR output .
.TP
.BI "write\-boot " "disk input" " \fR[\fIsector\fR [\fIlength\fR]]"
Write the host file
.I input
to the boot area, from sector
.I sector
(default 0).
With
.IR length ,
write that number of sectors, and fill with zeros after the end of the file.
.TP
.BI "verify " disk
Check the directory: each entry has a user number from 0 to 31 (or E5h for
a free entry) and a valid name, the extents of each file are complete, no
block belongs to two files, and each block is inside the disk and outside the
directory.
.SH OPTIONS
Each command accepts these options, and each command but
.B create
accepts
.BR \-\-slice :
.TP
.B \-\-sssd
The image is an SSSD floppy.
.TP
.B \-\-combo
The image is a combo disk.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-skew
SSSD only: no sector interleave.
Some emulators use images with no interleave.
.TP
.BI \-\-slice " N"
The slice of a combo image, 0 to 5 (default 0).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the help of the command and exit.
.PP
Some commands accept more options:
.TP
.BR \-\-force ", " \-f
.BR create :
write over a file that exists.
.TP
.BR \-\-sys ", " \-s
.BR add :
set the SYS attribute, so that the files show in every user area.
.TP
.BR \-\-user ", " \-u " \fIUSER\fR"
.B add
and
.BR extract :
the user area, 0 to 15 (default 0).
.TP
.BR \-\-output ", " \-o " \fIDIR\fR"
.BR extract :
the host directory for the files (default: the current directory).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command worked.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed.
.TP
.B 2
The command line is not correct: an unknown option, a missing argument, or a
.B \-\-slice
that the image does not have.
.SH EXAMPLES
Make an 8MB hd1k image and put two programs in it:
.PP
.RS
.B cpm_disk create disk.img
.br
.B cpm_disk add disk.img mbasic.com stat.com
.RE
.PP
List slice 3 of a combo image:
.PP
.RS
.B cpm_disk list \-\-slice 3 combo.img
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cpmemu (1),
.BR cpmls (1)
(from cpmtools)
.PP
https://github.com/avwohl/cpmemu
